From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm: TF_GLM_OVN_ONEPASS_PIPE, the one-pass pipeline with bit-exact switches

ai-engine a63e56649 grafted onto 0016. glm_onepass_pipe.cu / .cuh and
glm_onepass_common.cuh carry the pipeline (TensorFold-derived, attribution kept in the
headers, single-lined); cuda_onepass gains pipe_smem, wantedPipe, takesExact and
runPipe; the DSA block calls it ahead of the SPARSE_ONEPASS hook, and glue.Set plus
Modules carry the optional PipeKernels. Knob off: openPipe returns null, every launch
unchanged.

Pin adaptations: headBlock takes one argument at the pin (rows), so takesExact calls it
that way; the DSA block's parameter is k.set; PipeKernels' entry function at the pin is
`chunk`, so Set's onepass_pipe takes x.chunk; the ONEPASS_EXACT Set line is left out
because the pin's glue.Kernels has no such kernel (that lever rides its own patch); the
Modules field `tiled` (absent in the source's literal) is kept so the engine's
assignment still compiles.

Gates on pin+0001..0017: check-native-cuda-host green, test-lane-api-host green,
whole-tree fmt green, lean base-vs-head 0 new, fatbins green for the new .cu files.

Folded in by the 2026-11-12 fold (work/fold/MAP.tsv), each hunk where it belongs:
- 0028: the exact test's wide-tile floor is this base's
- 0029: the sparse-attention launch 0016 duplicated goes, one call a pass (its hunks sit on the form this patch gives the DSA block)
